01:04:08.900 --> 01:04:11.960
Couldn't figure out what it was for like a month.

1556
01:04:11.960 --> 01:04:13.360
Oh, this is so disgusting.

1557
01:04:13.660 --> 01:04:14.640
It's so disgusting.

1558
01:04:14.860 --> 01:04:21.580
And then there's a certain point where the smell really zeroes in on one area and he finally

1559
01:04:21.580 --> 01:04:24.380
lift the back thing and it was so foul.

1560
01:04:24.640 --> 01:04:27.500
It was like maggots and disgustingness.

1561
01:04:27.680 --> 01:04:33.160
He wasn't noticing that like the water in his toilet was affected?

1562
01:04:33.540 --> 01:04:34.640
I don't know what to tell you, lady.

1563
01:04:34.800 --> 01:04:35.720
I don't know what to tell you.

1564
01:04:35.880 --> 01:04:37.580
Did Nick find this amusing?

1565
01:04:38.200 --> 01:04:39.520
Oh, it was on.

1566
01:04:39.900 --> 01:04:42.820
After that, it really, the pranking got really out of control.

1567
01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:44.240
They got really into pranking.

1568
01:04:44.640 --> 01:04:46.040
Here's my thing about pranking.

1569
01:04:46.140 --> 01:04:46.440
What?

1570
01:04:46.840 --> 01:04:50.280
For me personally, to like get through a day.

1571
01:04:50.460 --> 01:04:50.640
Yeah.

1572
01:04:51.020 --> 01:04:56.660
Just with my own thoughts in my head and everything life is throwing at me.

1573
01:04:56.720 --> 01:04:57.000
Yes.

1574
01:04:57.160 --> 01:04:58.140
You know what I don't need?

1575
01:04:58.280 --> 01:04:58.800
A prank.

1576
01:04:58.980 --> 01:04:59.520
Your prank.

1577
01:04:59.740 --> 01:04:59.900
Yeah.

1578
01:05:07.860 --> 01:05:11.880
And you were specifically supposed to do a joke gift.

1579
01:05:12.100 --> 01:05:12.280
Right.

1580
01:05:12.640 --> 01:05:17.460
And I had to come up with like a joke Christmas present.

1581
01:05:18.240 --> 01:05:22.640
So what I did was the roommate of the person's name who I picked.

1582
01:05:22.780 --> 01:05:22.980
Yeah.

1583
01:05:23.120 --> 01:05:28.020
I said over the course of one month, will you slowly just sort of steal things from your

1584
01:05:28.020 --> 01:05:29.620
roommate like a single shoe?

1585
01:05:29.860 --> 01:05:31.740
Like I gave him a list of things.

1586
01:05:31.800 --> 01:05:32.780
Oh, yours is a slow play.

1587
01:05:33.000 --> 01:05:33.400
Yeah.

1588
01:05:33.400 --> 01:05:39.820
I was just like, have little things go missing, like maybe favorite coffee mug, and then at

1589
01:05:39.820 --> 01:05:45.660
the very end, toothbrush, and then at the Christmas party, I had wrapped up all of the missing

1590
01:05:45.660 --> 01:05:49.220
items into a box, and then that was the gift.

1591
01:05:49.760 --> 01:05:50.700
Oh, that's kind of fun.

1592
01:05:50.720 --> 01:05:52.860
It was all your stuff that's gone missing for a month.

1593
01:05:53.060 --> 01:05:53.300
Yeah.

1594
01:05:53.640 --> 01:05:54.760
That was my joke gift.

1595
01:05:54.900 --> 01:05:55.640
I like that.

1596
01:05:55.800 --> 01:05:57.420
I am not much of a prankster.

1597
01:05:57.560 --> 01:05:58.600
I'm a lame pranker.

1598
01:05:58.960 --> 01:06:02.760
Well, I'm glad you're a lame pranker lady because I don't want pranks in my life,

1599
01:06:02.760 --> 01:06:07.740
and you're my BFF, and so I'm happy they don't have a BFF that is like devoted to pranking.

1600
01:06:07.940 --> 01:06:09.720
Yeah, that would really suck, wouldn't it?

1601
01:06:09.760 --> 01:06:10.400
It really would.

1602
01:06:11.060 --> 01:06:15.020
I have a location breakdown for Alfredo's Pizza Cafe.

1603
01:06:15.480 --> 01:06:16.320
Let's hear it.

1604
01:06:16.460 --> 01:06:22.440
This was a restaurant in Woodland Hills, California called Nicola's, and it is owned by a husband

1605
01:06:22.440 --> 01:06:26.000
and wife that we're friends with our set designer, Michael Gallenberg.

1606
01:06:26.340 --> 01:06:26.740
Oh.

1607
01:06:26.980 --> 01:06:31.420
And Randy said that we did not have to do much redressing of this restaurant at all.

1608
01:06:31.420 --> 01:06:34.720
We were able to pretty much just use it as it was.

1609
01:06:34.980 --> 01:06:35.860
That's great.

1610
01:06:36.200 --> 01:06:41.900
Randy would also like you to know that Nicola's has the best chopped salad in the valley.

1611
01:06:42.240 --> 01:06:43.020
I looked it up.

1612
01:06:43.200 --> 01:06:45.420
It looks really good, and it costs $16.

1613
01:06:46.040 --> 01:06:47.800
I would love a chopped salad right now.

1614
01:06:47.920 --> 01:06:48.420
I know.

1615
01:06:48.700 --> 01:06:49.980
That's what we should do after.

1616
01:06:50.200 --> 01:06:51.740
Let's swing by Nicola's or something.

1617
01:06:51.940 --> 01:06:52.660
And have a chopped salad?

1618
01:06:52.760 --> 01:06:53.400
Have a chopped salad.

1619
01:06:53.400 --> 01:06:59.200
Well, in order to shoot this scene, we had to get there at 6.30 in the morning, and we

1620
01:06:59.200 --> 01:07:03.480
had to shoot at 7.30 because we had to do it before the restaurant was open.

1621
01:07:04.400 --> 01:07:06.880
But after this, BJ and I just got to go home.

1622
01:07:06.940 --> 01:07:08.000
That's all I had to do that day.

1623
01:07:08.080 --> 01:07:09.760
I remember I was back home by like 10 a.m.

1624
01:07:09.900 --> 01:07:11.120
My work day was done.

1625
01:07:11.960 --> 01:07:14.800
Steve and the rest of the crew did a whole day of locations.

1626
01:07:15.260 --> 01:07:21.140
But while I was looking at the call sheet, I saw this fascinating detail, which was the

1627
01:07:21.140 --> 01:07:22.200
van schedule.

1628
01:07:22.700 --> 01:07:23.040
Ooh.

1629
01:07:23.540 --> 01:07:27.100
Do you remember these van schedules when we would shoot on Location Lady?

1630
01:07:27.680 --> 01:07:28.080
No.

1631
01:07:28.540 --> 01:07:29.340
You don't?

1632
01:07:29.420 --> 01:07:33.620
Oh, see, this is the thing I used to love to do where I read every detail of a call

1633
01:07:33.620 --> 01:07:33.960
sheet.

1634
01:07:34.140 --> 01:07:34.640
Yes, you would.

1635
01:07:35.080 --> 01:07:37.760
I would show up and be like, why is Access Hollywood here?

1636
01:07:37.920 --> 01:07:39.840
And you'd be like, Angela, it's on the call sheet.

1637
01:07:40.160 --> 01:07:43.260
And they put a memo in your trailer probably last week.

1638
01:07:43.380 --> 01:07:44.120
I stepped right over that piece of paper.

1639
01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:44.820
She really would.

1640
01:07:44.920 --> 01:07:46.860
There'd be a pile of memos on her floor.

1641
01:07:47.060 --> 01:07:47.800
I'd kick the papers to the side.

1642
01:07:48.000 --> 01:07:48.340
All right.

1643
01:07:48.460 --> 01:07:53.060
So when you shoot on Location, you park your car and they have the hair and makeup trailers

1644
01:07:53.060 --> 01:07:55.500
in a big parking lot and they call it Base Camp.

1645
01:07:56.000 --> 01:07:58.680
This is where the caterers will set up their food tent.

1646
01:07:58.680 --> 01:07:59.840
It's where you eat lunch.

1647
01:08:00.280 --> 01:08:04.800
But a lot of times Base Camp is really far away from the actual shooting location.

1648
01:08:04.800 --> 01:08:06.420
And that was the case here.

1649
01:08:06.620 --> 01:08:12.200
It was about a 15-minute van ride to get from Base Camp to Nicola's Restaurant.

1650
01:08:12.200 --> 01:08:17.260
So they had to have a van schedule to shuttle all of these people to set.

1651
01:08:17.460 --> 01:08:18.680
And here's what it said.

1652
01:08:18.960 --> 01:08:26.240
It said breakfast would be available as of 5.15 and then you could take one of six vans to set.

1653
01:08:26.240 --> 01:08:33.080
They left at 5.42 a.m., 6.00 a.m., 6.12 a.m.

1654
01:08:33.220 --> 01:08:38.220
And they designated this van for our grip and electric crew, 6.30 a.m.

1655
01:08:38.700 --> 01:08:42.800
And then there was one last van at 6.42 a.m.

1656
01:08:42.940 --> 01:08:45.860
And in all caps, it said, this is the late van.

1657
01:08:46.520 --> 01:08:48.300
You did not want to be on the late van.

1658
01:08:48.440 --> 01:08:48.600
Don't do it.

1659
01:08:49.100 --> 01:08:49.720
No, no, no, no.

1660
01:08:50.060 --> 01:08:56.680
There were also additional shuttles for the cast and the background actors that were set to leave at 7 a.m.

1661
01:08:57.080 --> 01:09:01.560
So the idea was the crew would get there, set up all the lights, and then the actors would land.

1662
01:09:01.820 --> 01:09:03.900
The hair and makeup folks would ride with the actors.

1663
01:09:04.280 --> 01:09:05.360
That's the van schedule.

1664
01:09:05.360 --> 01:09:08.160
That was Randy's job to make that van schedule.

1665
01:09:08.440 --> 01:09:09.500
He did a fantastic job.

1666
01:09:09.940 --> 01:09:12.000
So Dwight never makes it to the restaurant.

1667
01:09:12.000 --> 01:09:13.680
He calls and says he hit a bear.

1668
01:09:14.260 --> 01:09:16.940
And Michael just believes it.

1669
01:09:17.100 --> 01:09:18.100
Not just Michael.

1670
01:09:18.440 --> 01:09:21.520
I will have you know that Pam and Ryan don't even raise an eyebrow.

1671
01:09:21.720 --> 01:09:26.840
They don't even look up from their menu when Michael says Dwight hit a bear, but he's on the way.

1672
01:09:27.240 --> 01:09:28.980
How many bears has Dwight hit?

1673
01:09:29.200 --> 01:09:30.920
Why is this so believable?

1674
01:09:31.420 --> 01:09:33.560
They get back to Michael Scott Paper Company.

1675
01:09:33.560 --> 01:09:35.500
They discover they've been robbed.

1676
01:09:35.900 --> 01:09:36.620
Dwight calls.

1677
01:09:36.800 --> 01:09:38.940
Michael is like, I don't have time to talk.

1678
01:09:39.080 --> 01:09:40.080
We've been robbed.

1679
01:09:40.900 --> 01:09:44.400
And once again, Pam and Ryan are like, it was Dwight.

1680
01:09:44.720 --> 01:09:45.100
Yeah.

1681
01:09:45.420 --> 01:09:49.220
This is when Dwight is going to start poaching the clients off the Rolodex.

1682
01:09:49.380 --> 01:09:55.620
And to get back at him, Michael is going to eat his meatball parm that he brought back for him, which is so funny.

1683
01:09:55.620 --> 01:09:57.980
He goes, Dwight says, I knew you were going to do that.

1684
01:09:58.120 --> 01:10:01.740
And that's why I made you order it because it's the worst thing on their menu.

1685
01:10:02.120 --> 01:10:05.140
And then the way Steve is so disgusted by it.

1686
01:10:05.300 --> 01:10:09.200
Why is it so funny to watch Steve eat food that he's disgusted with?

1687
01:10:09.340 --> 01:10:09.480
Anything with food.

1688
01:10:09.800 --> 01:10:10.400
It's hilarious.

1689
01:10:10.740 --> 01:10:13.120
Well, in Casual Friday, he's going to eat everybody's lunch.

1690
01:10:13.120 --> 01:10:14.040
And it's very, very funny.

1691
01:10:14.140 --> 01:10:15.000
I can't wait to get to that.

1692
01:10:15.100 --> 01:10:16.540
There's some good bloopers from that, too.

1693
01:10:17.020 --> 01:10:18.680
Listen, there was a deleted scene.

1694
01:10:18.880 --> 01:10:23.360
As Dwight is poaching everyone's clients, he really crosses the line with Ryan.

1695
01:10:24.700 --> 01:10:29.680
Because Ryan's uncle chooses Dwight over the Michael Scott Paper Company.

1696
01:10:29.920 --> 01:10:30.120
What?

1697
01:10:30.420 --> 01:10:30.580
Yeah.

1698
01:10:30.720 --> 01:10:32.280
And there's some really good Pam sass.

1699
01:10:32.400 --> 01:10:33.120
We got to hear it.

1700
01:10:33.980 --> 01:10:35.780
Dwight just got Howard family dry cleaners.

1701
01:10:36.840 --> 01:10:37.600
Uncle Dave?

1702
01:10:37.720 --> 01:10:39.480
Little jerk is undercutting us big time.

1703
01:10:39.700 --> 01:10:43.540
He is actually taking a loss and paying the difference out of pocket.

1704
01:10:43.680 --> 01:10:44.420
That's my family.

1705
01:10:45.400 --> 01:10:48.880
When you mess with my family, I can't be responsible for my actions.

1706
01:10:49.540 --> 01:10:51.600
When are you ever responsible for your actions?

1707
01:10:51.720 --> 01:10:52.760
Get off my ass, you hag.

1708
01:10:52.760 --> 01:10:53.580
Hey, hey, hey.

1709
01:10:53.740 --> 01:10:55.080
Something about that seems inappropriate.

1710
01:10:56.600 --> 01:10:58.880
Something about that seems inappropriate.

1711
01:10:58.980 --> 01:11:00.580
He can't put his finger on it.

1712
01:11:00.800 --> 01:11:04.140
I love the Ryan-Pam rivalry.

1713
01:11:04.420 --> 01:11:06.020
I just live for it.

1714
01:11:06.520 --> 01:11:07.700
I love it, too.

1715
01:11:08.120 --> 01:11:12.200
I mean, I just loved working with these guys for this period of time.

1716
01:11:12.300 --> 01:11:13.540
I bet it was so much fun.

1717
01:11:13.540 --> 01:11:23.740
Well, now we're going to get into a pretty fun bit where Michael is going to walk in to HarperCollins with Dwight on the phone.

1718
01:11:23.900 --> 01:11:27.020
He's like, I'm going to let you listen to me still, your biggest client.

1719
01:11:27.440 --> 01:11:30.440
And Dwight's like, no, and takes off.

1720
01:11:30.440 --> 01:11:33.280
And he gets in the car all the while listening.

1721
01:11:33.700 --> 01:11:35.320
That was so funny.

1722
01:11:35.460 --> 01:11:38.540
Rain in the car when he was like, paper is the manure.

1723
01:11:39.280 --> 01:11:40.300
And on time.

1724
01:11:42.150 --> 01:11:43.730
I wrote down that quote, too.

1725
01:11:44.190 --> 01:11:45.470
Do I need that on a mug?

1726
01:11:45.630 --> 01:11:46.990
We might need it on a mug.

1727
01:11:47.150 --> 01:11:48.370
Paper is the manure.

1728
01:11:50.190 --> 01:11:52.470
We had a fan question from Sydney S.

1729
01:11:52.610 --> 01:11:57.190
who said, how did you guys film that scene of Dwight driving to Mr. Schofield's office?

1730
01:11:57.450 --> 01:11:59.570
Was Steve really on the other end of the phone?

1731
01:12:00.470 --> 01:12:02.970
No, Steve was not on the other end of the phone.

1732
01:12:03.710 --> 01:12:05.850
And I talked with Randy about this.

1733
01:12:06.450 --> 01:12:07.770
Rain is really driving.

1734
01:12:08.030 --> 01:12:08.890
He's free driving.

1735
01:12:09.130 --> 01:12:10.770
He is not hooked up to anything.

1736
01:12:10.970 --> 01:12:13.750
It looked like it to me, just the way he pulled into the parking lot.

1737
01:12:13.970 --> 01:12:15.330
Yeah, the whole time.

1738
01:12:15.330 --> 01:12:18.710
So they had LAPD officers on motorcycles.

1739
01:12:19.150 --> 01:12:22.490
So no one would sort of interfere with the shot or rain driving.

1740
01:12:22.790 --> 01:12:23.470
Yes, correct.

1741
01:12:23.850 --> 01:12:26.790
And there's also a crew van following behind.

1742
01:12:27.210 --> 01:12:28.970
But here's how they got that shot.

1743
01:12:29.430 --> 01:12:31.990
Matt Soane, our camera operator, was in the front seat.

1744
01:12:32.370 --> 01:12:32.890
Oh.

1745
01:12:33.010 --> 01:12:33.670
Filming rain.

1746
01:12:34.090 --> 01:12:37.530
Our sound engineer, Ben Patrick, was in the back seat recording sound.

1747
01:12:37.710 --> 01:12:40.690
And our director, Paul Feig, was also in the back seat.

1748
01:12:40.990 --> 01:12:43.190
That was not a big back seat.

1749
01:12:43.310 --> 01:12:44.610
I have been in that car.

1750
01:12:44.610 --> 01:12:45.990
That is tiny.

1751
01:12:46.290 --> 01:12:46.850
I know.

1752
01:12:47.270 --> 01:12:50.790
And Randy said, we did not have a two-way phone setup.

1753
01:12:51.050 --> 01:12:52.630
It was just too unreliable.

1754
01:12:52.910 --> 01:12:59.370
And so Randy's guess is that Paul Feig was reading Steve's dialogue so that Rain could react to it.

1755
01:12:59.450 --> 01:12:59.630
Yeah.

1756
01:13:00.110 --> 01:13:00.550
Amazing.

1757
01:13:00.970 --> 01:13:03.070
I wish we had a picture of those four guys in the car.

1758
01:13:03.370 --> 01:13:07.130
Can we talk about what happens when Dwight arrives at Mr. Schofield's office?

1759
01:13:07.390 --> 01:13:07.830
Finally.

1760
01:13:07.830 --> 01:13:09.250
I lived for this.

1761
01:13:09.450 --> 01:13:12.850
I had to know if this was scripted or improvised.

1762
01:13:13.010 --> 01:13:15.050
So Dwight is going to run in.

1763
01:13:15.170 --> 01:13:17.370
First of all, he's changing into his mustard shirt.

1764
01:13:17.490 --> 01:13:18.330
I loved that detail.

1765
01:13:18.550 --> 01:13:19.210
I loved that detail.

1766
01:13:19.430 --> 01:13:23.450
And then when he gets to the receptionist, he does this crazy spin move.

1767
01:13:23.450 --> 01:13:26.110
And then Dwight says spin move.

1768
01:13:26.350 --> 01:13:28.610
And I was like, did Rain improvise that?

1769
01:13:28.750 --> 01:13:29.330
I've got to know.

1770
01:13:29.670 --> 01:13:31.250
Jenna, it was 100% in the script.

1771
01:13:31.870 --> 01:13:32.310
Everything.

1772
01:13:32.690 --> 01:13:33.790
Even the spin move.

1773
01:13:33.970 --> 01:13:34.450
All of it.

1774
01:13:34.450 --> 01:13:40.650
I found an old interview with Rain where he said that one time he did a somersault.

1775
01:13:41.590 --> 01:13:44.950
And he said he thought that it would look extra stealthy.

1776
01:13:45.150 --> 01:13:45.330
Yeah.

1777
01:13:45.470 --> 01:13:50.470
When they watched it back, it looked, quote, like a manatee doing ballet at SeaWorld.

1778
01:13:51.890 --> 01:13:54.410
He also said they did about five takes.

1779
01:13:54.850 --> 01:13:59.330
I also have a little guest star breakdown for Mr. Schofield's receptioniSt.

1780
01:13:59.330 --> 01:14:07.230
She was played by Angela Campola-Sanders, who was our casting associate on The Office since season four.

1781
01:14:07.450 --> 01:14:09.070
This is her only acting credit.

1782
01:14:09.290 --> 01:14:09.610
That's awesome.

1783
01:14:09.610 --> 01:14:12.630
But she played Mr. Schofield's receptioniSt.

1784
01:14:12.870 --> 01:14:16.810
Pretty much everyone in our casting office made it into the episode at some point.

1785
01:14:16.910 --> 01:14:17.490
I love that.

1786
01:14:17.650 --> 01:14:18.110
I do too.

1787
01:14:18.790 --> 01:14:26.010
Dwight is about to dig himself into a big old hole because he doesn't understand Michael's Rolodex or Michael's color coding info.

1788
01:14:26.010 --> 01:14:29.770
Michael has a talking head where he says, I color code all my info.

1789
01:14:29.950 --> 01:14:31.170
I wrote gay son in green.

1790
01:14:31.370 --> 01:14:32.110
Green means go.

1791
01:14:32.310 --> 01:14:34.350
So I know to go ahead and shut up about it.

1792
01:14:34.850 --> 01:14:35.130
Yes.

1793
01:14:35.210 --> 01:14:37.510
And orange means orange you glad you didn't bring it up.

1794
01:14:37.750 --> 01:14:39.390
Most colors mean don't say it.

1795
01:14:39.830 --> 01:14:40.070
Yeah.

1796
01:14:40.430 --> 01:14:41.570
But Dwight doesn't know that.

1797
01:14:42.230 --> 01:14:42.530
Yeah.

1798
01:14:42.690 --> 01:14:47.410
So Dwight is basically saying all the things that are color coded to not be said.

1799
01:14:47.610 --> 01:14:47.810
Right.

